"name\":\"cc-plugin-telemetry\",\"path\":\"builtin\",\"source\":\"cc-plugin-telemetry@builtin\"}],\"capabilities\":[\"interrupt_receipt_v1\",\"interrupt_cancel_queued_v1\",\"msg_lifecycle_v1\",\"mcp_read_resource_v1\",\"mcp_tool_ui_meta_v1\"],\"analytics_disabled\":false,\"product_feedback_disabled\":false,\"uuid\":\"fd188b60-b4ee-457f-81ae-730ed01e8c41\",\"memory_paths\":{\"auto\":\"/Users/davidbean/.claude/projects/-Users-davidbean-Projects-attest/memory/\"},\"messaging_socket_path\":\"/tmp/cc-socks/49528.sock\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"fast_mode_disabled_reason\":\"sdk_opt_in_required\",\"per_turn_effort_active\":false,\"view_mode\":\"default\"}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"diagnostics\":null,\"id\":\"266f0b6b-bbec-429d-a076-d547bbe52760\",\"container\":null,\"model\":\"<synthetic>\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"stop_details\":null,\"stop_reason\":\"stop_sequence\",\"stop_sequence\":\"\",\"type\":\"message\",\"usage\":{\"output_tokens_details\":null,\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":0,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":null,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":null,\"iterations\":null,\"speed\":null,\"fallback_credit\":null},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Failed to authenticate: OAuth session expired and could not be refreshed\"}],\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"41f43776-bdba-41e1-89cb-f18de4482f30\",\"uuid\":\"d6603fec-6284-4574-807d-2fe6a8126739\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-30T00:56:29.885Z\",\"error\":\"authentication_failed\",\"is_api_error_message\":true}\n[adapter exited 1]## Problem\n\nClass: core\n\nThe issue is the unit of work (ruled 2026-09-29). The plan in the store (#264) orders issues and says nothing else about them: an issue's title, whether it is open, when it closed, its labels, and the paths it claims before it has a spec all live in the forge. The product cannot read any of them. `frontier.py`, session tooling outside the product, reads open issues with `gh` directly. The screen's unclassed queue calls `gh` itself. Epic progress (closed issues over all issues under an epic) and the waves (which open issues can start, given their claims) both need this read, and the product names no vendor.\n\nThe product already reads the forge through commands the tenant declares: `checks_command`, `check_log_command`, `file_issue_command` and `attestation_command`. This item adds a fifth, `[forge].issues_command`. It takes nothing and prints the tenant's issues, open and closed, as one JSON list of `{number, title, state, closed_at, labels, body}`.\n\n`attavo/issues.py` runs it, bounded at 60 s by `run_bounded`, and returns the issues in number order. Each issue's `claims` are parsed from its body's `## Claims` section: one `- path` line each, up to the next `## ` heading, with backticks stripped. An issue with no such section has `claims` None, which is not the same as a section that lists nothing. The product parses the claims, not the tenant's command, so every tenant's issues are read by one rule.\n\nA read that cannot be made is \"not read\" with its reason, never an empty list:\n\n- no command in the manifest;\n- a non-zero exit, with the command's last stderr line;\n- a run past its bound;\n- output that is not JSON;\n- an entry of the wrong shape, including a state other than `open` or `closed`, which is how the forge's own `OPEN` would show if a tenant's command passed it through.\n\nThis repository declares `issues_command = \"python3 .attavo/bin/forge-issues\"`. That script calls `gh issue list --state all` and translates the forge's words (upper-case states, label objects) into the shape. It exits non-zero with nothing on stdout when the forge cannot be read, or when the list would be cut at its limit.\n\nThe schema declares the new key, and the forge description no longer says there are two keys. `tests/test_record_schemas.py` counts the `json.loads(` sites under `attavo/`: the count moves from 11 to 12, and its docstring names this one (the issues as the command prints them, never a record). The selector maps `attavo/issues.py` and `.attavo/bin/forge-issues` to `tests/test_issues.py`.\n\nNothing reads `read_issues` yet. `attavo frontier` (FR) is its first reader, and the screen's unclassed queue can move onto it afterwards. FI is filed ahead of FR so FR's stub stands on a merged read.\n\nThe stub under `stub/` is the change on `5df6926`: the module, the script, the manifest line, the schema key, the selector lines, the count, and seven tests in `tests/test_issues.py`, all red on `5df6926`. `python3 -m mypy` exits 0 on the change. The suite passes on it, except four doctor proofs that read this repository's own history, which a scratch copy cannot supply; they fail identically on `5df6926` there.\n\nRetires: `gh` calls to read issues outside the product, first `frontier.py --github`'s issue read, once FR reads through this; and an issue's Claims section as prose that nothing in the product parses.\n\n## Claims\n\n- attavo/issues.py\n- .attavo/bin/forge-issues\n- .attavo/bin/select-tests\n- attavo.toml\n- schema/manifest.schema.json\n- tests/test_issues.py\n- tests/test_record_schemas.py\n\n## Criteria\n\n- the-product-reads-issues-and-their-claims-through-the-tenants-command.sh: this repository's `forge-issues`, with a stand-in `gh` on PATH, prints two issues that `read_issues` reads in number order, with states lower-cased, label names, the Claims of the one whose body has a section (backticks stripped, the Acceptance line left out) and None for the other; no command reads \"not read: no [forge].issues_command\", and a command exiting 4 reads \"not read: [forge].issues_command exited 4\"; `attavo.toml` declares the command and the schema names the key; and `tests/test_issues.py` carries the seven tests named\n{\n  \"read\": true,\n  \"reason\": null,\n  \"checks\": []\n}\n## the default branch, first-parent, since this item's branch point\n\n(nothing new)\n\n## this branch's own commits since the branch point\n\n93f25239de943ed5c4e6f4eec75ff1453687e88b attavo driver attavo: build invocation 02 started for item 267\n890eee56c61663683e46a65b698061847b1f0a2d attavo driver attavo: build record for item 267 (build-01)\n22831ee93aa5d72a3a761ddea8cfb1895e24b8d7 attavo driver attavo: build invocation 01 started for item 267\n5338f44ae770bbe6e81848cd66f3610864383e92 David Bean attavo: approval record for item 267\n243a9c2190795c432fa08662722648349a71ebcf attavo-records[bot] attavo: spec-gate record for item 267\n9f328be47311b149144abe7c4722ef5006130040 David Bean spec for #267: the product reads issues through [forge].issues_command\n\n## markers and records present at 93f25239de943ed5c4e6f4eec75ff1453687e88b\n\nattest/records/267/approval-01.json\nattest/records/267/build-01.filed\nattest/records/267/build-01.json\nattest/records/267/build-01.log\nattest/records/267/build-01.started\nattest/records/267/build-02.started\nattest/records/267/counsel-01.json\nattest/records/267/counsel-01.log\nattest/records/267/spec-01.json\n\n## check runs for the last three shas on this branch\n\n93f25239de943ed5c4e6f4eec75ff1453687e88b: (no checks)\n890eee56c61663683e46a65b698061847b1f0a2d: action-self-check=success, schema-version=success, test=in_progress, doctor=in_progress, typecheck=success, spec-gate=success, coherence=in_progress\n22831ee93aa5d72a3a761ddea8cfb1895e24b8d7: coherence=success, test=in_progress, schema-version=success, doctor=in_progress, typecheck=success, action-self-check=success, spec-gate=successschema_version = 1\n\n[attavo]\nversion = \"v0.30.0\"\n\n[forge]\nchecks_command = \"python3 .attavo/bin/forge-checks\"\ncheck_log_command = \"python3 .attavo/bin/forge-check-log\"\nfile_issue_command = \"python3 .attavo/bin/file-issue\"\nattestation_command = \"sh .attavo/bin/forge-attestation\"\nsealed_since = \"83fcbc6863fdb65956b77768c66c2103d221521b\"\n\n[executor]\nbuild = \"claude-code\"\nverify = \"codex\"\n\n[executor.claude-code]\nauth = \"subscription\"\nmodel = \"claude-sonnet-5\"\n\n[executor.codex]\nmodel = \"gpt-5.6-sol\"\n\n[spec]\n[spec.boundary]\npaths = [\"bin/**\", \"attavo/**\", \"adapters/**\", \"schema/**\", \"templates/**\", \"action.yml\", \"scripts/**\"]\n\n[gates]\n[gates.spec]\ncommand = \"attavo spec-gate\"\nretires = [\n  \"the lane as the product's transport: a Claude Code lane session reporting to a reviewing session, with no spec, no approval bound to a commit, no build/verify separation, and no attestation on the product's own commits\",\n  \"the || true step in ci.yml that ran the doctor's four proofs against this repository expected to still fail\",\n  \"the reviewing session as the reader of whether the lane did what the issue said\",\n]\n\n[tests]\nselect = \"python3 .attavo/bin/select-tests\"\ncall_timeout_s = 240\nrun = \"xargs -r python3 -m pytest -q -m 'not own_records'\"\n\n[paths]\nspecs = \"attest/specs\"\nrecords = \"attest/records\"\nrulings = \"attest/rulings.md\"\nrejections = \"attest/rejections\"\n\n[doctor]\nbuilt_since = \"dae6d765f3d6\"\n\n[operators]\napprovers = [\"dbean10\"]\n\n[checks]\ncommand = \"python3 -m mypy\"\nprobe = \"python3 -c 'import pytest, mypy, jsonschema'\"\nprobe_timeout_s = 60\n\n[drive]\nstall_after_s = 1800\nattempts = 3\nretry_after_s = 300\n\n[drive.build]\nceiling_s = 3600\n\n[drive.verify]\nceiling_s = 1200\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
